{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"name":"ir","display_name":"R","language":"R"},"language_info":{"name":"R","codemirror_mode":"r","pygments_lexer":"r","mimetype":"text/x-r-source","file_extension":".r","version":"4.0.5"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"none","dataSources":[{"sourceId":4800245,"sourceType":"datasetVersion","datasetId":2777134}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"r","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":4,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"source":"<a href=\"https://www.kaggle.com/code/sergemoisan/superstore-marketing-v3?scriptVersionId=173416724\" target=\"_blank\"><img align=\"left\" alt=\"Kaggle\" title=\"Open in Kaggle\" src=\"https://kaggle.com/static/images/open-in-kaggle.svg\"></a>","metadata":{},"cell_type":"markdown"},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# This R environment comes with many helpful analytics packages installed\n# It is defined by the kaggle/rstats Docker image: https://github.com/kaggle/docker-rstats\n# For example, here's a helpful package to load\n\nlibrary(tidyverse) # metapackage of all tidyverse packages\n\n# Input data files are available in the read-only \"../input/\" directory\n# For example, running this (by clicking run or pressing Shift+Enter) will list all files under the input directory\n\nlist.files(path = \"../input\")\n\n# You can write up to 20GB to the current directory (/kaggle/working/) that gets preserved as output when you create a version using \"Save & Run All\" \n# You can also write temporary files to /kaggle/temp/, but they won't be saved outside of the current session","metadata":{"_uuid":"051d70d956493feee0c6d64651c6a088724dca2a","_execution_state":"idle","execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:08.167614Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:08.173989Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:09.055996Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## About this Dataset\n### Context\nA superstore is planning for the year-end sale. They want to launch a new offer - gold membership, that gives a 20% discount on all purchases, for only \\$ $ 499\\$ which is  999$ on other days. It will be valid only for existing customers and the campaign through phone calls is currently being planned for them. The management feels that the best way to reduce the cost of the campaign is to make a predictive model which will classify customers who might purchase the offer.\n### Objective\nThe superstore wants to predict the likelihood of the customer giving a positive response and wants to identify the different factors which affect the customer's response. You need to analyze the data provided to identify these factors and then build a prediction model to predict the probability of a customer will give a positive response.\n\n\n## Data Description\n\n- Response (target) - 1 if customer accepted the offer in the last campaign, 0 otherwise\n- ID - Unique ID of each customer\n- YearBirth - Age of the customer Complain - 1 if the customer complained in the last 2 years\n- DtCustomer - date of customer's enrollment with the company\n- Education - customer's level of education\n- Marital - customer's marital status\n- Kidhome - number of small children in customer's household\n- Teenhome - number of teenagers in customer's household\n- Income - customer's yearly household income\n- MntFishProducts - the amount spent on fish products in the last 2 years\n- MntMeatProducts - the amount spent on meat products in the last 2 years\n- MntFruits - the amount spent on fruits products in the last 2 years\n- MntSweetProducts - amount spent on sweet products in the last 2 years\n- MntWines - the amount spent on wine products in the last 2 years\n- MntGoldProds - the amount spent on gold products in the last 2 years\n- NumDealsPurchases - number of purchases made with discount\n- NumCatalogPurchases - number of purchases made using catalog (buying goods to be shipped through the mail)\n- NumStorePurchases - number of purchases made directly in stores\n- NumWebPurchases - number of purchases made through the company's website\n- NumWebVisitsMonth - number of visits to company's website in the last month\n- Recency - number of days since the last purchase\n\nLet's first get the data.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"options(repr.plot.width = 22, repr.plot.height = 12)\nsuperstoredata <- read_csv('/kaggle/input/superstore-marketing-campaign-dataset/superstore_data.csv')\nhead(superstoredata)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:12.42006Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:12.421682Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:12.884043Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"summary(superstoredata)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:16.403566Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:16.405133Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:16.434407Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"str(superstoredata)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:19.081975Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:19.083581Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:19.141762Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"library('psych')\ndescribe(superstoredata)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:22.572458Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:22.575115Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:22.795377Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Missing values","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoredata %>%\n  map_dbl(~sum(is.na(.)))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:29.590344Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:29.59192Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:29.610427Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"There are 24 Income missing values.\nWe see that Id must be removed from the data. Complain is not correlated with response.\nThe date of birth can be changed to give the age of customer.\nEducation, Marital Status must be changed to factors and Dt_Customer changed to customer_age.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoredata <- superstoredata %>%\n  na.omit()\nsuperstoredata <- superstoredata[,!names(superstoredata) %in% c('Id','Complain')]\nsuperstoredatanewEducation <- as.factor(superstoredata$Education)\nsuperstoredata$Marital_Status <- as.factor(superstoredata$Marital_Status)\nsuperstoredata$Response <- as.factor(superstoredata$Response)\nsuperstoredata <- superstoredata %>%\n  mutate(age = 2022 - Year_Birth)\nsuperstoredata <- superstoredata %>%\n  mutate(Dt_Customer_1 = as.Date(Dt_Customer, format = \"%m/%d/%Y\")) %>%\n  mutate(loyalty = 2022 - year(Dt_Customer_1))\nsuperstoredata <- superstoredata[,!names(superstoredata) %in% c('Dt_Customer','Dt_Customer_1','Year_Birth')]\ndescribe(superstoredata)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:32.589038Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:32.590672Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:32.748467Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Some of the customers have given their real year of birth.\nWe shall eliminate those whose age is above 80 years for example and look at the distribution of ages","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoredata <-  superstoredata %>%\n  filter(age <= 80)\ndescribe(superstoredata)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:41.672666Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:41.674509Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:41.81968Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Correlations","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"library('GGally')\nggcorr(superstoredata, hjust = 1, layout.exp = 2, label = T, label_size = 2.9)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:47.442865Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:47.444455Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:48.365004Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Numerical Variables","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstore_numeric_data <- superstoredata %>%\n  dplyr::select(where(is.numeric))\nsuperstore_numeric_data <- superstore_numeric_data %>%\n  cbind(superstoredata$Response) %>%\n  rename(\"Response\" = \"superstoredata$Response\")\n\nsuperstoreData_gather <- superstore_numeric_data %>%\n  gather(key = \"Variable\", value = \"Value\", -Response)\n#superstoreData_gather\n\n\nsuperstoreData_gather %>%\n  #filter(Variable != \"Id\" & Variable != \"Dt_Customer\" & Variable != \"Complain\") %>%\n  ggplot(aes(factor(Response),Value,colour = factor(Response))) +\n  facet_wrap(~Variable, scales = \"free_y\") +\n  geom_boxplot(draw_quantiles = c(0.25,0.5,0.75)) +\n  theme_bw()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:52.49093Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:52.492697Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:37:55.270895Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":" We see that:\n\n  - The Income values are up to 600000 and can be limited to 200000 \n  - Some variables should be treated as factors: Kidhome, Teenhome and Loyalty.\n  \n\n### Boxplots\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoredata <- superstoredata %>%\n  filter(Income <= 200000)\nsuperstoredata$Kidhome <- as.factor(superstoredata$Kidhome)\nsuperstoredata$Teenhome <- as.factor(superstoredata$Teenhome)\nsuperstoredata$loyalty <- as.factor(superstoredata$loyalty)\n\nsuperstore_numeric_data <- superstoredata %>%\n  dplyr::select(where(is.numeric))\nsuperstore_numeric_data <- superstore_numeric_data %>%\n  cbind(superstoredata$Response) %>%\n  rename(\"Response\" = \"superstoredata$Response\")\n\nsuperstoreData_gather <- superstore_numeric_data %>%\n  gather(key = \"Variable\", value = \"Value\", -Response)\n\nsuperstoreData_gather %>%\n  ggplot(aes(factor(Response),Value,colour = factor(Response))) +\n  facet_wrap(~Variable, scales = \"free_y\") +\n  geom_boxplot(draw_quantiles = c(0.25,0.5,0.75)) +\n  theme_bw()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:37:59.618971Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:37:59.6207Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:38:02.020663Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"  ### Correlations with ggpairs:","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"library('GGally')\nggpairs(superstore_numeric_data, ggplot2::aes(colour=Response))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:38:06.137953Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:38:06.139524Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:38:50.52998Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":" Let's see the categorical variables: Education, Marital_Status, Kidhome, Teenhome, loyalty ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"library('dplyr')\nsuperstore_categorical_data <- superstoredata %>%\n  dplyr::select_if(negate(is.numeric))\ndescribe(superstore_categorical_data)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:39:32.922252Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:39:32.923946Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:39:33.008207Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Education Variable\nMaster and 2nd Cycle are equivalent","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoredata$Education[superstoredata$Education == '2n Cycle'] <- 'Master'\nsuperstoredata %>%\n  ggplot(aes(x = Education, fill = Response)) +\n  geom_bar()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:39:40.370335Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:39:40.371994Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:39:40.925912Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Marital Status Variable","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoredata %>%\n  ggplot(aes(x = Marital_Status, fill = Response)) +\n  geom_bar()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:40:28.271099Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:40:28.272724Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:40:28.853476Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"We discard \"Absurd\" and \"YOLO\" (single ?).\nAlone, divorced and widow are equivalent to single.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoredata$Marital_Status[superstoredata$Marital_Status %in% \nc('Alone','Divorced','Widow')] <- 'Single'\n\nsuperstoredata$Marital_Status[superstoredata$Marital_Status %in% \nc('Together')] <- 'Married'\n\nsuperstoredata <- superstoredata %>%\n  filter(Marital_Status != 'Absurd')\nsuperstoredata <- superstoredata %>%\n  filter(Marital_Status != 'YOLO')\n\nsuperstore_categorical_data <- superstoredata %>%\n  dplyr::select_if(negate(is.numeric))\n\nsuperstore_numeric_data <- superstoredata %>%\n  dplyr::select(where(is.numeric))\nsuperstore_numeric_data <- superstore_numeric_data %>%\n  cbind(superstoredata$Response) %>%\n  rename(\"Response\" = \"superstoredata$Response\")\n\nsuperstoredata %>%\n  ggplot(aes(x = Marital_Status, fill = Response)) +\n  geom_bar()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:41:56.024188Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:41:56.027758Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:41:56.901704Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### KidHome","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoredata %>%\n  ggplot(aes(x = Kidhome, fill = Response)) +\n  geom_bar()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:42:10.053385Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:42:10.055283Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:42:10.573714Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoredata %>%\n  ggplot(aes(x = loyalty, fill = Response)) +\n  geom_bar()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:42:15.479017Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:42:15.480738Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:42:15.99873Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Density Plots","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"library('cowplot')\nplot_xdensity <- function(variable3){\n  ggplot(superstore_numeric_data, aes_string(variable3, fill=\"Response\")) + \n  geom_density(alpha=.5) + \n  scale_fill_manual(values = c('#999999','#E69F00'))}\n\nplot_grid(ncol = 2,\n  plot_xdensity(\"Income\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"MntWines\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"MntFruits\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"MntMeatProducts\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"MntFishProducts\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"MntSweetProducts\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"MntGoldProds\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"Recency\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"NumDealsPurchases\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"NumWebPurchases\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"NumCatalogPurchases\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"NumStorePurchases\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"NumWebVisitsMonth\"),\n  plot_xdensity(\"age\")\n  )","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:42:32.005968Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:42:32.00786Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:42:36.32612Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Normalization","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"library('bestNormalize')\nlibrary('parallel')\nlibrary('parallelMap')\n\nsuperstore_numeric_data_normalized <- as_tibble(data.frame(matrix(nrow=nrow(superstore_numeric_data),ncol=0)))\n\nparallelStartSocket(cpus = detectCores())\nfor (i in 1:(ncol(superstore_numeric_data)-1)){\n  x <- superstore_numeric_data[,i]\nx_normalized <- bestNormalize(x,allow_lambert_s = TRUE)\nx <- predict(x_normalized) %>%\n  tibble()\nsuperstore_numeric_data_normalized <- superstore_numeric_data_normalized %>%\n  cbind(x)\n}\nparallelStop()\n\nsuperstore_numeric_data_normalized <- superstore_numeric_data_normalized %>%\n  cbind(superstore_numeric_data$Response)\n\ncolnames(superstore_numeric_data_normalized) <- colnames(superstore_numeric_data)\n\nplot_xdensity_normalized <- function(variable4){\n  ggplot(superstore_numeric_data_normalized, aes_string(variable4, fill=\"Response\")) + \n  geom_density(alpha=.5) + \n  scale_fill_manual(values = c('#999999','#E69F00'))}\n\nplot_grid(ncol = 2,\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"Income\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"MntWines\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"MntFruits\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"MntMeatProducts\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"MntFishProducts\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"MntSweetProducts\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"MntGoldProds\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"Recency\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"NumDealsPurchases\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"NumWebPurchases\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"NumCatalogPurchases\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"NumStorePurchases\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"NumWebVisitsMonth\"),\n  plot_xdensity_normalized(\"age\")\n)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:44:00.193657Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:44:00.195406Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:44:54.593876Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Categorical Variables Encoding","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#Encode the categorical variables\nencode_ordinal <- function(x, order = unique(x)) {\n  x <- as.numeric(factor(x, levels = order, exclude = NULL))\n  x\n}\n\ntable(superstoredata[[\"Education\"]], encode_ordinal(superstoredata[[\"Education\"]]), useNA = \"ifany\")\nsuperstoredata[[\"Education_encoded\"]] <- encode_ordinal(superstoredata[[\"Education\"]])\nsuperstoredata[[\"Marital_encoded\"]] <- encode_ordinal(superstoredata[[\"Marital_Status\"]])\nsuperstoredata_enc <- superstoredata[,!names(superstoredata) %in% c('Education', 'Marital_Status')]\nsuperstoredata_enc$Kidhome = as.numeric(superstoredata_enc$Kidhome)\nsuperstoredata_enc$Teenhome = as.numeric(superstoredata_enc$Teenhome)\nsuperstoredata_enc$loyalty = as.numeric(superstoredata_enc$loyalty)\ndescribe(superstoredata_enc)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:45:35.555955Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:45:35.557705Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:45:35.714803Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Modelization with knn","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Modelizations with mlr package\n#### 1 - Feature Importance","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"install.packages('FSelector')\nlibrary('FSelector')\n#Feature importance\nim_feat <- generateFilterValuesData(superstoreTask, method = c(\"information.gain\"))\nplotFilterValues(im_feat,n.show = 20)\n\nim_feat <- generateFilterValuesData(superstoreTask, method = c(\"chi.squared\"))\nplotFilterValues(im_feat,n.show = 20)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:49:17.8779Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:49:17.881865Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:50:35.091526Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### 2 - kNN","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"library('mlr')\n## Using mlr to train k-NN model\n\n# load metrics package\nlibrary('Metrics')\n# Get the Recall\n# The Recall, also known as TPR, True Positive Rate, is a metrics to measure the performance of a binary classification system.\n# It is computed as the ratio between the truly positive predictions and the real positive values.\n# In other words, the TPR is the measure of the system capacity to identify the true positive values. \n\n\nsuperstoreTask <- makeClassifTask(data = superstoredata_enc,target = \"Response\")\nsuperstoreTask\n\n# Define a learner\nknn <- makeLearner(\"classif.knn\", par.vals=list(\"k\" = 2))\n# listLearners()$class\n# listLearners(\"classif\")$class","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T18:54:46.18003Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T18:54:46.18233Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T18:54:46.313084Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"The positive class here is 0. Let's modify it:\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"superstoreTask <- makeClassifTask(data = superstoredata_enc,target = \"Response\",positive = \"1\")\nsuperstoreTask\n\n# Define a learner\nknn <- makeLearner(\"classif.knn\", par.vals=list(\"k\" = 2))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T19:17:23.672739Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T19:17:23.675286Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T19:17:23.737648Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"The dataset is very imbalanced (1870 ","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### 2.1 - Training Performance and plot","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Train the model\nknnModel <- train(knn,superstoreTask)\n\n#Predict\nknnPred <- predict(knnModel,newdata=superstoredata_enc)\n\n#Measure the performance\nperformance(knnPred,measures = list(mmce,acc,tpr))\n","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T19:17:29.263156Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T19:17:29.267403Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T19:17:29.407998Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"TPR is 0.64. Is it overfitting?","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# PlotLearnerPrediction (from https://rpubs.com/ippromek/336804)\nlearnerKNN=makeLearner(id=\"KNN\",\"classif.knn\")\n\nplotLearnerPrediction(\n  learnerKNN,\n  superstoreTask,\n  features = c(\"Income\", \"MntWines\"),\n  cv = 100L,\n  gridsize = 100\n) + scale_fill_manual(values = c(\"#ff0061\", \"#11a6fc\", \"#ffae00\")) + theme_bw()\n\n#Using Cross validation to train our knn model\nholdout <- makeResampleDesc(method=\"Holdout\", split = 2/3, stratify = TRUE)\nholdoutCV <- resample(learner = knn, task = superstoreTask, resampling = holdout,measures = list(mmce,acc,tpr))\nholdoutCV$aggr\n\n# Confusion Matrix\ncalculateConfusionMatrix(holdoutCV$pred,relative= TRUE)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T19:18:19.455781Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T19:18:19.457425Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T19:18:20.549911Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"TPR is now 0.18 !","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### 2.2 - Cross Validation","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# k fold cross validation\nkFold <- makeResampleDesc(method = \"RepCV\", folds= 10, reps =50,stratify = TRUE)\nkFoldCV <- resample(learner = knn, task = superstoreTask, resampling = kFold, measures = list(mmce,acc,tpr))\nkFoldCV$aggr\n\n# Confusion Matrix\ncalculateConfusionMatrix(kFoldCV$pred,relative= TRUE)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T19:20:41.701567Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T19:20:41.703442Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T19:20:53.291237Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"TPR equals 0.27. This has to be improved","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### 2.3 - Leave_One_Out","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#Leave one out CV\nLOO <- makeResampleDesc(method = \"LOO\")\nLOOCV <- resample(learner = knn, task = superstoreTask, resampling = LOO, measures = list(mmce,acc,tpr))\nLOOCV$aggr\n\n# Confusion Matrix\ncalculateConfusionMatrix(LOOCV$pred,relative= TRUE)\n","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-22T19:21:47.916322Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-22T19:21:47.918239Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-22T19:22:17.077702Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"We see in the confusion matrix 194 errors on predicted values = 1 as the true values were 0.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Tuning k:\nknnParamSpace <- makeParamSet(makeDiscreteParam(\"k\",values = 5:18))\ngridSearch <- makeTuneControlGrid()\ncvForTuning <- makeResampleDesc(\"RepCV\", folds= 10, reps = 20)\ntunedK <-\n  tuneParams(\n    \"classif.knn\",\n    task = superstoreTask,\n    resampling = cvForTuning,\n    par.set = knnParamSpace,\n    control = gridSearch\n  )\ntunedK\ntunedK$x","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-21T09:26:06.235016Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-21T09:26:06.236754Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-21T09:26:57.262929Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#Visualisation\nknnTuningData <- generateHyperParsEffectData(tunedK)\nplotHyperParsEffect(knnTuningData,x=\"k\",y=\"mmce.test.mean\",plot.type = \"line\")+\n  theme_bw()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-21T09:27:02.940382Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-21T09:27:02.942145Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-21T09:27:03.413677Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#Let's use the k = 11 parameter\ntunedKnn <- setHyperPars(makeLearner(\"classif.knn\",par.vals = tunedK$x))\ntunedKnnModel <- train(tunedKnn,superstoreTask)\n\n#Predict\ntunedKnnPred <- predict(tunedKnnModel,newdata=superstoredata_enc)\n\n#Measure the performance\nperformance(tunedKnnPred,measures = list(mmce,acc,tpr))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-21T09:27:36.440417Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-21T09:27:36.443201Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-21T09:27:36.713136Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Including hyperparameter tuning in the CV\ninner <- makeResampleDesc(\"CV\")\nouter <- makeResampleDesc(\"RepCV\",folds=10,reps=5)\nknnWrapper <- makeTuneWrapper(\"classif.knn\",resampling = inner,\n                              par.set = knnParamSpace,control = gridSearch)\ncvWithTuning <- resample(knnWrapper,superstoreTask,resampling = outer)\ncvWithTuning\ncvWithTuning$aggr","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-21T09:28:06.574244Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-21T09:28:06.577898Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-21T09:30:13.022984Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(knnWrapper)\nknnWrapperModel = train(knnWrapper, task = superstoreTask)\nknnWrapperModel\n\n#Confusion Matrix\ncalculateConfusionMatrix(cvWithTuning$pred,relative = TRUE)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-21T09:31:41.423196Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-21T09:31:41.425056Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-21T09:31:44.467672Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#Training the decision tree model\ntree <- makeLearner(\"classif.rpart\")\nmap_dbl(superstoredata_enc, ~sum(is.na(.)))\n\ngetParamSet(tree)\n\ntreeParamSpace <- makeParamSet(\n  makeIntegerParam(\"minsplit\", lower = 5, upper = 20),\n  makeIntegerParam(\"minbucket\", lower = 3, upper = 10),\n  makeNumericParam(\"cp\", lower = 0.01, upper = 0.1),\n  makeIntegerParam(\"maxdepth\", lower = 1,upper = 10)\n)\n\nrandSearch <- makeTuneControlRandom(maxit = 200)\ncvForTuning <- makeResampleDesc(\"CV\",iters = 5)\n\nlibrary('parallel')\nlibrary('parallelMap')\n\nparallelStartSocket(cpus = detectCores())\ntunedTreePars <- tuneParams(tree, task = superstoreTask,\n                            resampling = cvForTuning,\n                            par.set = treeParamSpace,\n                            control = randSearch)\nparallelStop()\ntunedTreePars\n\n# Training the model with the tuned hyperparametes\ntunedTree <- setHyperPars(tree, par.vals = tunedTreePars$x)\ntunedTreeModel <- train(tunedTree,superstoreTask)\n\n#Plotting the decision tree\nlibrary('rpart.plot')\ntreeModelData <- getLearnerModel(tunedTreeModel)\nrpart.plot(treeModelData, roundint = FALSE,\n           box.palette = \"BuBn\",\n           type = 5)","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-21T09:32:56.739475Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-21T09:32:56.741324Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-21T09:33:40.146652Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"#Exploring the model\nprintcp(treeModelData,digits = 3)\n\nsummary(treeModelData)\n\n# Cross validating the decision tree model\nouter <- makeResampleDesc(\"CV\", iters = 5)\ntreeWrapper <- makeTuneWrapper(\"classif.rpart\",resampling = cvForTuning,\n                               par.set = treeParamSpace,\n                               control = randSearch)\n\nparallelStartSocket(cpus = detectCores())\ncvWithTuning <- resample(treeWrapper, superstoreTask,resampling = outer)\nparallelStop()","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-21T09:34:01.259554Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-21T09:34:01.261681Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-21T09:36:58.749727Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Extracting the result\ncvWithTuning\ncvWithTuning$aggr","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-21T09:37:11.354512Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-21T09:37:11.356321Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-21T09:37:11.404851Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":"ranger.lrn = makeLearner(cl = \"classif.ranger\",  # class of learner\n                         predict.type = \"response\", # prediction output type\n                         par.vals = list(num.threads = 8), # set hyperparameters\n                         predict.threshold = NULL, # threshold for prediction\n                         fix.factors.prediction = TRUE)\n                         #id = 'bc ranger') # add a factor level for missing data in test\nranger.lrn\n\nlearners <- listLearners(superstoreTask, properties = 'prob', check.packages = FALSE)\nDT::datatable(learners[,c('class', 'package')])\n\nranger_model <- train(learner = ranger.lrn, \n                  task = superstoreTask)\nranger_model\n\nranger_pred <- predict(object = ranger_model,\n                   newdata=superstoredata_enc)\n\n#Measure the performance\nperformance(ranger_pred,measures = list(mmce,acc,tpr))","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2024-04-21T09:37:33.097316Z","iopub.execute_input":"2024-04-21T09:37:33.09904Z","iopub.status.idle":"2024-04-21T09:37:35.358635Z"},"trusted":true},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}]}